  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Players take turns playing one card. The played card may capture one card of equal value, or a set of table cards whose values sum to the played card's value. In Scopa Corse capturing is optional: a player may leave a card on the table even if it could capture. Clearing the table scores a scopa (1 point). After each round of plays, new cards are dealt. Play and scoring otherwise match basic Scopa.",
    Player: "Players take turns playing one card. The played card may capture one card of equal value, or a set of table cards whose values sum to the played card's value. In Scopa Corse capturing is optional: a player may leave a card on the table even if it could capture. Clearing the table scores a scopa (1 point). After each round of plays, new cards are dealt. Play and scoring otherwise match basic Scopa.",
    objective: 'Capture cards from the table by playing a card that matches a single table card or the sum of a set; score for most cards, most coins, settebello, primiera, and sweeps. First to 21 points wins.',
    gameplay: "Players take turns playing one card. The played card may capture one card of equal value, or a set of table cards whose values sum to the played card's value. In Scopa Corse capturing is optional: a player may leave a card on the table even if it could capture. Clearing the table scores a scopa (1 point). After each round of plays, new cards are dealt. Play and scoring otherwise match basic Scopa.",
    keyRules: [
      '36-card deck with no 2s.',
      'Capturing is optional (unlike basic Scopa).',
      'Target score usually 21; may be 16 or 11 by agreement.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
